From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:40:12 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: instant modes in the command bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As in Arc and Raycast, the answer is the first row while typing and
Return copies it or acts:
- Calculator: functions (sqrt, sin, log, ln, abs…), constants (pi, e),
  "200 + 10%", 5!, 30°, "3 x 4", shown as "= 8".
- Currencies: the National Bank of Georgia's rates join the ECB's
  (GEL, RUB, AMD…), currency names and signs ("50€ in gel", "10 dollars
  in lari"), kept 12 hours and on disk for when offline (with their
  day), "Rates unavailable" otherwise.
- Time: "tokyo time", "3pm in tokyo", more cities.
- Translate: "translate hello to georgian", "tr привет" open Google
  Translate with the text.
- Site search by name then Tab ("youtube ⇥ cats"): Chromium's engine
  when there is one for the site, otherwise Meridian's table; a
  "Search YouTube ⇥" row offers it.
- Commands by name: Split View, Little Window, Boost This Site, Pin,
  New Folder, Welcome Tour (appended); "settings ai" opens Settings at AI.

Fixes "the command bar finds Settings": picking a place in Settings no
longer hands the keys back to the page, which raced Settings for focus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
